invariant: INV-51
file: Makefile
catches: test/docker-aes-runtime-qemu.sh sha512-avx2
reason: unit_cflags, which hands -fno-schedule-insns2 to the two rules that
  compile sha512_avx2.c, returns nothing, so gcc compiles the kernel for
  x86-64 with its second scheduling pass on in the packaged object and in
  every test binary. The variable that holds the flag is as it was. The
  kernel computes the same digests, leaves the same stack and clears the
  same registers, so bin/sha2_equiv_test and the published vectors pass.
  The lane's sha512-avx2 part runs make lint-schedule-order-gcc under its
  gcc for x86-64, which reads the assembly the two rules' commands write
  and finds 99 instructions on general registers between two vector
  instructions where a round is 30. The lane builds with that gcc on
  every machine, so the verdict is the same on each. It skips without
  docker, and this then reports unguarded rather than caught.

--- old
unit_cflags = $(if $(filter sha512_avx2.c,$(1)),$(SHA512_AVX2_GCC_CFLAGS))
--- new
unit_cflags =
